# SGLang settings for this machine only. .env is ignored by git, so nothing in
# it ends up in the public repo. ./set_model.sh creates .env from this file for
# you, admin key included; or copy it yourself:
#   cp .env.template .env
# After a change, Start the service again (manage.sh -> Start) to apply it.

# The model SGLang serves - the one setting SGLang cannot guess. ./set_model.sh
# lists the models downloaded with stack/downloaders/huggingface and writes your choice here.
HUGGINGFACE_MODEL=""

# Locks SGLang's management functions, such as swapping the model's weights or
# loading add-ons, so nothing else on the shared Docker network can use them.
# Chats don't need it and neither do you, so ./set_model.sh fills in a random
# one. SGLang won't start without it. Its log shows the key when it starts:
# remove it before you share a log.
SGLANG_ADMIN_API_KEY=""

# Everything below is optional.

# Share of the GPU's memory SGLang keeps for the model and its working memory,
# from 0 to 1. By default SGLang works it out from the size of the GPU. Lower
# it to leave room for something else on the GPU.
#VRAM_LIMIT=0.8

# Longest conversation in tokens, input plus output. By default the longest
# the model supports. A number caps it, e.g. 32768.
#CONTEXT_SIZE=32768

# Extra SGLang options, written as you would type them after
# "python3 -m sglang.launch_server". A model's page on huggingface.co often
# lists the ones it needs. For example, when the log says it "could not detect"
# a model's tool calls, name the format yourself:
#SGLANG_EXTRA_ARGS="--tool-call-parser qwen3_coder"
# Qwen3.5-family models (Qwen3.6, Qwen3.8, Ornith) keep extra memory for each
# conversation. On a 32 GB card that runs out and SGLang restarts over and over
# ("state cache is too small"); storing it at half precision fixes that:
#SGLANG_EXTRA_ARGS="--mamba-ssm-dtype bfloat16"
# Some models only run with --trust-remote-code. That runs Python code that came
# with the model download, so only add it for a model from a source you trust.

# Port on this PC (default 30000). Change it if something else already uses it.
#SGLANG_PORT=30000

# SGLang release. The default is the one this repo is set up with. Pick a newer
# one from https://hub.docker.com/r/lmsysorg/sglang/tags, e.g.
# "v0.5.22-runtime", or "latest-runtime" for the newest with every Update.
#SGLANG_IMAGE_TAG=v0.5.21-runtime
